#> tool: sedrepl
#> wait: Mont@n@
#> pause: 40
#> must: Al@b@m@
#> must: Iowa
#> must: K@ns@s
#> not: Iow@
#> not: ERROR parsing
#> source: /Iowa/!s
# 9. Substitute everywhere EXCEPT on lines that match. Pement: sed '/baz/!s/foo/bar/g'
# An address in front of s limits it to matching lines; ! after the address
# flips that, so the substitution runs on every line that does not match.
# Here every "a" becomes "@" except on the Iowa line, which keeps its own.
# Try: drop the ! and only Iowa changes.
/Iowa/!s/a/@/g

#DATA
Alabama
Alaska
Iowa
Kansas
Montana
